# vr-profile.conf -- per-person calibration read by jack-in-wayland.sh.
#
# Copy to ~/vr/vr-profile.conf and put your own numbers in. Not tracked with real values,
# because these are physical properties of a person, not of the project.
#
# WHAT TO MEASURE: the height of your EYES off the floor, in metres, in the posture you
# actually play in. Not your stature -- eyes sit roughly 11 cm below the top of the head,
# and sitting down changes it by far more than that.
#
# Easiest way to get it right: stand (or sit) as you would to play, have someone measure
# from the floor to the outer corner of your eye. A tape against a wall and a pencil mark
# works as well. Being within a centimetre or two is plenty; the current default is a
# hardcoded 1.6 m for everyone, so almost any real measurement is an improvement.
#
# WHY IT MATTERS: Monado never measures the floor. It places the STAGE space a hardcoded
# 1.6 m below wherever the headset is when tracking starts, so the world is built assuming
# your eyes are exactly there. Seated, that is out by around half a metre -- the floor ends
# up near your knees and everything sits too high.
#
# Which of the two is used comes from VR_POSTURE (standing|seated, default standing):
#
#     VR_POSTURE=seated ./jack-in-wayland.sh 1 6dof
#
# VR_EYE_HEIGHT_M=<metres> in the environment overrides both, for measuring.

EYE_HEIGHT_STANDING_M=1.60
EYE_HEIGHT_SEATED_M=1.20
